    "success_condition": "Continue after R-079 at A13-CLASSII-FUTURE-CONTROL-WEIGHTED-INNOVATION-BRACKET. R-079 closes the exact complete frame-current and canonical safe-packet Doob decomposition into a conditional low-current boundary, present-control increments, and future-control innovations while retaining the present/future cross term and the complete low endpoint. It proves a spatially weighted Cameron--Martin square function that spends strict-past control energy once and an exact backward-heat projection for the base or predictably translated current. The terminal feedback commutator still contains both coefficient and derivative-feedback channels. Generic Cauchy plus the weighted square function has Young deficit -4/15; expected budgets do not imply conditional BMO, and generic spatial-gain and adapted Wick carre-du-champ positivity shortcuts fail. These are method no-gos, not production counterexamples. Prove the production near/far commutator estimate inside the complete R-079 identity and the resulting weighted packet lower bound; then apply R-075 fixed-cutoff graph recovery, assemble controlled-shell one-use, and return to q=10/9 Nelson synthesis. Sector A remains open."
  },
